ich allows us to combine title-level information with cast and crew information for further analysis.\n","\n","During the initial data inspection, duplicate records and missing values were identified in the datasets. These issues will be handled during the **data wrangling and data cleaning** stage before performing exploratory data analysis.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"gfoNAAC-nUe_"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## ***2. Understanding Your Variables***"],"metadata":{"id":"nA9Y7ga8ng1Z"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Dataset Columns\n","titles_df.columns"],"metadata":{"id":"j7xfkqrt5Ag5"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["credit_df.columns"],"metadata":{"id":"LOYErNOnTjr2"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Dataset Describe\n","titles_df.describe(include='all')"],"metadata":{"id":"DnOaZdaE5Q5t"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Variables Description"],"metadata":{"id":"PBTbrJXOngz2"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### 2. Understanding Your Variables\n","\n","The **Titles dataset** contains information about movies and TV shows, including their basic details, ratings, popularity, genres, and production information. The description of each variable is given below:\n","\n","| Variable               | Description                                                                            |\n","| ---------------------- | -------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n","| `id`                   | Unique identifier assigned to each movie or TV show.                                   |\n","| `title`                | Name of the movie or TV show.                                                          |\n","| `type`                 | Specifies whether the title is a Movie or a TV Show.                                   |\n","| `description`          | Provides a brief summary or description of the movie or TV show.                       |\n","| `release_year`         | Year in which the movie or TV show was released.                                       |\n","| `age_certification`    | Age rating or certification assigned to the title.                                     |\n","| `runtime`              | Duration of the movie or TV show content, measured in minutes.                         |\n","| `genres`               | Genre or genres associated with the movie or TV show.                                  |\n","| `production_countries` | Country or countries where the movie or TV show was produced.                          |\n","| `seasons`              | Number of seasons available for a TV show. This is generally not applicable to movies. |\n","| `imdb_id`              | Unique identifier of the title on IMDb.                                                |\n","| `imdb_score`           | Rating or score given to the title on IMDb.                                            |\n","| `imdb_votes`           | Number of votes received by the title on IMDb.                                         |\n","| `tmdb_popularity`      | Popularity score of the title on TMDB.                                                 |\n","| `tmdb_score`           | Rating or score given to the title on TMDB.                                            |\n"],"metadata":{"id":"aJV4KIxSnxay"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The **Credits dataset** contains information about the people involved in each movie or TV show, including actors, characters, and their roles.\n","\n","| Variable    | Description                                                                                                                     |\n","| ----------- | ------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |\n","| `person_id` | Unique identifier assigned to each person in the credits dataset.                                                               |\n","| `id`        | Unique identifier of the corresponding movie or TV show. It can be used to connect the Credits dataset with the Titles dataset. |\n","| `name`      | Name of the person involved in the movie or TV show.                                                                            |\n","| `character` | Name of the character portrayed by the person.                                                                                  |\n","| `role`      | Indicates the person's role in the movie or TV show, such as actor or director.                                                 |\n"],"metadata":{"id":"BkB7Pn56T5VJ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Check Unique Values for each variable."],"metadata":{"id":"u3PMJOP6ngxN"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Check Unique Values for each variable in titles\n","for column in titles_df.columns.tolist():\n","    print(f\"\\n{column}: {titles_df[column].nunique()}\")"],"metadata":{"id":"zms12Yq5n-jE"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["for column in credit_df.columns.tolist():\n","    print(f\"\\n{column}: {credit_df[column].nunique()}\")"],"metadata":{"id":"3cVHst4VVL_Y"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["\n","## 3. ***Data Wrangling***"],"metadata":{"id":"dauF4eBmngu3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### Data Wrangling Code"],"metadata":{"id":"bKJF3rekwFvQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["####Create a copy of the raw datasets"],"metadata":{"id":"ck3I628ycAam"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["titles_clean = titles_df.copy()\n","credits_clean = credit_df.copy()"],"metadata":{"id":"NNqiXLBBbwwT"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["####Check dataset dimensions"],"metadata":{"id":"F2Gy6m5XcNQv"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["titles_clean.shape"],"metadata":{"id":"Mspb_qXnb_bu"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["credits_clean.shape"],"me