ape)\n","print(\"Credits Shape:\", credits_clean.shape)\n","\n","print(\"\\nTitles Duplicates:\", titles_clean.duplicated().sum())\n","print(\"Credits Duplicates:\", credits_clean.duplicated().sum())\n","\n","print(\"\\nTitles ID Unique:\", titles_clean['id'].is_unique)\n","\n","print(\"\\nMissing Values - Titles\")\n","display(titles_clean.isnull().sum())\n","\n","print(\"\\nMissing Values - Credits\")\n","display(credits_clean.isnull().sum())"],"metadata":{"id":"iL-TGlk0y5U3"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### What all manipulations have you done and insights you found?"],"metadata":{"id":"MSa1f5Uengrz"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Finding 1 — Duplicate Records\n","\n","**Manipulation:**\n","Three duplicate records were identified and removed from the Titles dataset. 56 duplicate records were also identified in the Credits dataset.\n","\n","**Insight:**\n","Removing duplicates prevents the same records from being counted multiple times during analysis.\n","\n","---\n","\n","#### Finding 2 — Age Certification\n","\n","**Manipulation:**\n","Missing values in `age_certification` were replaced with `\"Unknown\"`.\n","\n","**Insight:**\n","This preserves the records while clearly identifying titles where certification information is unavailable.\n","\n","---\n","\n","#### Finding 3 — Seasons\n","\n","**Manipulation:**\n","Missing values in `seasons` were investigated based on the `type` of content.\n","\n","**Insight:**\n","All 8,511 missing season values belong to Movies, while TV Shows contain season information. Therefore, these values represent **Not Applicable (N/A)** and were retained as NaN instead of being replaced with 0.\n","\n","---\n","\n","#### Finding 4 — Numerical Variables\n","\n","**Manipulation:**\n","Numerical columns were analyzed using descriptive statistics to identify unusual values and understand their distributions.\n","\n","**Insight:**\n","\n","* `release_year` ranges from **1912 to 2022**.\n","* `imdb_score` ranges from **1.1 to 9.9**.\n","* `tmdb_score` ranges from **0.8 to 10**.\n","* `imdb_votes` and `tmdb_popularity` show a highly skewed distribution.\n","* `runtime` and `seasons` contain some unusually high values that require further investigation rather than automatic removal.\n","\n","---\n","\n","#### Finding 5 — Dataset Relationship\n","\n","**Manipulation:**\n","The `id` column was used to check the relationship between the Titles and Credits datasets.\n","\n","**Insight:**\n","Approximately **89.80% of Titles have corresponding credit information**, while **100% of Credits records match a title** in the Titles dataset. This confirms that the Credits dataset can be linked to the Titles dataset using `id`.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"LbyXE7I1olp8"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## ***4. Data Vizualization, Storytelling & Experimenting with charts : Understand the relationships between variables***"],"metadata":{"id":"GF8Ens_Soomf"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart 1: Movies vs TV Shows."],"metadata":{"id":"0wOQAZs5pc--"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 1 visualization code\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(7,5))\n","\n","sns.countplot(\n","    data=titles_clean,\n","    x='type'\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Distribution of Movies and TV Shows')\n","plt.xlabel('Content Type')\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Titles')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"7v_ESjsspbW7"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["titles_clean['type'].value_counts()"],"metadata":{"id":"PuhEqbNfY58C"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["titles_clean['type'].value_counts(normalize=True) * 100"],"metadata":{"id":"DhrEQ6eGY9BW"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"K5QZ13OEpz2H"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A count plot/bar chart was selected because type is a categorical variable. It clearly compares the number of Movies and TV Shows in the dataset."],"metadata":{"id":"XESiWehPqBRc"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"lQ7QKXXCp7Bj"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Movies dominate the dataset with 8,511 titles (86.25%), while TV Shows account for only 1,357 titles (13.75%). This shows that the available content is heavily concentrated on Movies."],"metadata":{"id":"C_j1G7yiqdRP"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"448CDAPjqfQr"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. This insight can help the business understand its content mix and make better content-planning decisions. The large share of Movies indicates a strong focus on movie content.\n","\n","This chart alone does not indicate negative growth, because it shows content distribution rather than changes in business performance over time. Further analysis of ratings, popularity, genres, and release trends is required before concluding whether the current content mix has a positive or negative impact on growth."],"metadata":{"id":"3cspy4FjqxJW"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart 2: Content Release Trend Over the Years"],"metadata":{"id":"KSlN3yHqYklG"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 2 visualization code\n","\n","release_trend = (\n","    titles_clean\n","    .groupby(['release_year', 'type'])\n","    .size()\n","    .reset_index(name='count')\n",")\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(12, 6))\n","\n","sns.lineplot(\n","    data=release_trend,\n","    x='release_year',\n","    y='count',\n","    hue='type'\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Release Trend of Movies and TV Shows Over the Years')\n","plt.xlabel('Release Year')\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Titles')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"R4YgtaqtYklH"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["release_trend.sort_values(\n","    'count',\n","    ascending=False\n",").head(10)"],"metadata":{"id":"t9pPE9zjciZA"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"t6dVpIINYklI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A line chart was chosen because it clearly shows how the number of Movies and TV Shows has changed over different release years and makes it easier to identify increasing or decreasing trends."],"metadata":{"id":"5aaW0BYyYklI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"ijmpgYnKYklI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["*   Movie releases show a strong increase in the later years.\n","*   The highest number of Movies in the dataset was 715 in 2021, followed by 703 in 2019 and 574 in 2020.\n","*   Overall, the dataset contains significantly more Movies than TV Shows, especially in recent years.\n","*   The trend indicates that Movies have contributed more heavily to the growth of available content in the dataset."],"metadata":{"id":"PSx9atu2YklI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"-JiQyfWJYklI"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. This insight can help in content planning and understanding changes in the content mix over time. The strong increase in Movie releases can help identify periods of higher content availability and support future content strategy. However, a decrease in releases in a particular year should not be treated as negative business growth by itself, because the chart only measures the number of titles released, not revenue, subscribers, or profitability."],"metadata":{"id":"BcBbebzrYklV"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart 3: Which age certifications are most common among the titles?"],"metadata":{"id":"EM7whBJCYoAo"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 3 visualization code\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","\n","sns.countplot(\n","    data=titles_clean,\n","    x='age_certification',\n","    order=titles_clean['age_certification'].value_counts().index\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Distribution of Titles by Age Certification')\n","plt.xlabel('Age Certification')\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Titles')\n","plt.xticks(rotation=45)\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"t6GMdE67YoAp"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"fge-S5ZAYoAp"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A bar chart was chosen because age certification is a categorical variable, and a bar chart makes it easy to compare the number of titles across different certification categories."],"metadata":{"id":"5dBItgRVYoAp"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"85gYPyotYoAp"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The most noticeable insight is that Unknown has the highest distribution among all age-certification categories. This means a large portion of the titles in the dataset does not have age-certification information available. The remaining titles are distributed across different certification categories."],"metadata":{"id":"4jstXR6OYoAp"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"RoGjAbkUYoAp"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. This insight can help identify a data-quality and content-classification issue. Having many titles with unknown certification can make it difficult to accurately identify and target specific audience groups. Improving the completeness of age-certification data could support better content categorization, audience targeting, and parental-control features. However, this does not directly indicate negative business growth; it represents a potential data-quality limitation.\n","\n"],"metadata":{"id":"zfJ8IqMcYoAp"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart 4: Top Genres by Number of Titles"],"metadata":{"id":"4Of9eVA-YrdM"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 4 visualization code\n","\n","# Convert genres from string representation into individual genres\n","from ast import literal_eval\n","\n","genres = titles_clean['genres'].apply(literal_eval)\n","\n","genre_counts = (\n","    genres\n","    .explode()\n","    .value_counts()\n","    .head(10)\n",")\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","\n","sns.barplot(\n","    x=genre_counts.values,\n","    y=genre_counts.index\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Top 10 Genres by Number of Titles')\n","plt.xlabel('Number of Titles')\n","plt.ylabel('Genre')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"irlUoxc8YrdO"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"iky9q4vBYrdO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A horizontal bar chart was chosen because there are multiple genre categories, and it makes it easier to compare the number of titles across the top genres."],"metadata":{"id":"aJRCwT6DYrdO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"F6T5p64dYrdO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The top three genres are Drama, Comedy, and Thriller. This shows that these genres have the highest representation in the dataset, indicating that they form a major part of the available content."],"metadata":{"id":"Xx8WAJvtYrdO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"y-Ehk30pYrdP"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. These insights can support content planning and audience targeting by showing which genres have the largest content presence. The lower representation of other genres may indicate opportunities to explore more diverse content. However, the chart alone cannot indicate negative business growth because it measures the number of titles, not viewer demand, revenue, or profitability."],"metadata":{"id":"jLNxxz7MYrdP"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart 5: Average IMDb Score by Content Type"],"metadata":{"id":"bamQiAODYuh1"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 5 visualization code\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(7, 5))\n","\n","sns.barplot(\n","    data=titles_clean,\n","    x='type',\n","    y='imdb_score',\n","    estimator='mean'\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Average IMDb Score by Content Type')\n","plt.xlabel('Content Type')\n","plt.ylabel('Average IMDb Score')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"TIJwrbroYuh3"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"QHF8YVU7Yuh3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A bar chart was chosen because it provides a simple comparison of the average IMDb score between Movies and TV Shows."],"metadata":{"id":"dcxuIMRPYuh3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"GwzvFGzlYuh3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The chart helps identify which content type has a higher average IMDb rating. It provides an overall view of the audience-rated quality of Movies compared with TV Shows."],"metadata":{"id":"uyqkiB8YYuh3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"qYpmQ266Yuh3"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. The comparison can help understand which content type receives better audience ratings, which may support content planning and quality-focused decisions. A lower average IMDb score for one content type can highlight an area where content quality or audience preferences may need further investigation. However, IMDb score alone does not directly measure business growth, revenue, or viewership."],"metadata":{"id":"_WtzZ_hCYuh4"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart 6: Distribution of IMDb Scores"],"metadata":{"id":"OH-pJp9IphqM"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 6 visualization code\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","\n","sns.histplot(\n","    data=titles_clean,\n","    x='imdb_score',\n","    bins=20,\n","    kde=True\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Distribution of IMDb Scores')\n","plt.xlabel('IMDb Score')\n","plt.ylabel('Number of Titles')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"kuRf4wtuphqN"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"bbFf2-_FphqN"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A histogram was chosen because it is suitable for understanding the distribution of a numerical variable. It helps us see how IMDb scores are spread across different score ranges and where most titles are concentrated."],"metadata":{"id":"loh7H2nzphqN"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"_ouA3fa0phqN"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The chart shows how IMDb scores are distributed across the titles. Most titles are concentrated around the middle-to-higher score range, while relatively fewer titles have very low or extremely high ratings. This helps us understand the overall rating pattern of the content available in the dataset."],"metadata":{"id":"VECbqPI7phqN"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"Seke61FWphqN"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. The distribution of IMDb scores can help identify the overall quality and audience reception of the content. A large concentration of titles with moderate-to-high ratings can indicate that the content library has generally positive audience ratings. Titles with very low ratings can be further investigated to understand potential content-quality issues. However, IMDb ratings alone cannot be used to conclude business growth because they do not directly measure viewership, revenue, or customer retention."],"metadata":{"id":"DW4_bGpfphqN"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart 7: IMDb Score Distribution by Content Type"],"metadata":{"id":"PIIx-8_IphqN"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 7 visualization code\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","\n","sns.boxplot(\n","    data=titles_clean,\n","    x='type',\n","    y='imdb_score'\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('IMDb Score Distribution by Content Type')\n","plt.xlabel('Content Type')\n","plt.ylabel('IMDb Score')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"lqAIGUfyphqO"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"t27r6nlMphqO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A box plot was chosen because it allows us to compare the distribution of IMDb scores between Movies and TV Shows. It shows the median, spread, and potential outliers of the ratings."],"metadata":{"id":"iv6ro40sphqO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"r2jJGEOYphqO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The chart helps compare the typical IMDb scores and variation between Movies and TV Shows. It also shows whether either content type has unusually low or high-rated titles (outliers). The median and spread indicate how consistently each content type is rated."],"metadata":{"id":"Po6ZPi4hphqO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"b0JNsNcRphqO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. Understanding the rating distribution can help identify differences in audience reception between Movies and TV Shows and support content-quality analysis. If one content type shows more low-rated titles or greater variation, those titles can be investigated further. However, these ratings alone do not indicate negative business growth because they do not directly measure viewership, revenue, or customer retention."],"metadata":{"id":"xvSq8iUTphqO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart 8: IMDb Score vs IMDb Votes"],"metadata":{"id":"BZR9WyysphqO"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 8 visualization code\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","\n","sns.scatterplot(\n","    data=titles_clean,\n","    x='imdb_votes',\n","    y='imdb_score',\n","    alpha=0.5\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('IMDb Score vs IMDb Votes')\n","plt.xlabel('Number of IMDb Votes')\n","plt.ylabel('IMDb Score')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"TdPTWpAVphqO"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"jj7wYXLtphqO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A scatter plot was chosen because it is suitable for analyzing the relationship between two numerical variables — IMDb votes and IMDb score. It helps identify whether titles with more votes tend to have higher or lower ratings.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"Ob8u6rCTphqO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"eZrbJ2SmphqO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The chart shows that IMDb votes are highly spread out, with a small number of titles receiving a very large number of votes. The IMDb scores are distributed across different vote levels, so a higher number of votes does not necessarily mean a higher IMDb score. This suggests that popularity and rating are not directly the same measure."],"metadata":{"id":"mZtgC_hjphqO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"rFu4xreNphqO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. This analysis can help distinguish between content popularity and content rating quality. Titles with many votes can indicate higher audience engagement, while the rating provides an indication of audience reception. If highly voted titles have lower ratings, it may be useful to investigate why popular content is receiving weaker ratings. However, IMDb votes are not the same as actual platform viewership, so this chart alone cannot establish positive or negative business growth."],"metadata":{"id":"ey_0qi68phqO"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart 9: Top 10 Actors by Number of Titles"],"metadata":{"id":"YJ55k-q6phqO"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 9 visualization code\n","\n","# Filter actors only\n","actors = credits_clean[credits_clean['role'] == 'ACTOR']\n","\n","# Count titles for each actor\n","top_actors = (\n","    actors.groupby('name')['id']\n","    .nunique()\n","    .sort_values(ascending=False)\n","    .head(10)\n",")\n","\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","\n","sns.barplot(\n","    x=top_actors.values,\n","    y=top_actors.index\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Top 10 Actors by Number of Titles')\n","plt.xlabel('Number of Titles')\n","plt.ylabel('Actor')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"B2aS4O1ophqO"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"gCFgpxoyphqP"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A horizontal bar chart was chosen because it makes it easy to compare the number of titles associated with different actors and clearly identify the top 10 actors."],"metadata":{"id":"TVxDimi2phqP"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"OVtJsKN_phqQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The chart identifies the actors who have appeared in the highest number of titles in the dataset. These actors have a stronger presence across the content library compared with other actors."],"metadata":{"id":"ngGi97qjphqQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"lssrdh5qphqQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. This insight can help understand which actors have a strong presence in the content library and can support content analysis and audience-focused content planning. However, the number of appearances alone does not prove that an actor drives higher viewership or revenue. Therefore, this chart does not directly indicate positive or negative business growth."],"metadata":{"id":"tBpY5ekJphqQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart 10: Content Distribution by Region/Country"],"metadata":{"id":"U2RJ9gkRphqQ"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Chart - 10 visualization code\n","\n","from ast import literal_eval\n","\n","# Convert production_countries from string to list\n","countries = titles_clean['production_countries'].apply(literal_eval)\n","\n","# Count titles by country\n","country_counts = (\n","    countries\n","    .explode()\n","    .value_counts()\n","    .head(10)\n",")\n","\n","# Plot top 10 countries\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 6))\n","\n","sns.barplot(\n","    x=country_counts.values,\n","    y=country_counts.index\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Top 10 Countries by Number of Titles')\n","plt.xlabel('Number of Titles')\n","plt.ylabel('Country')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"GM7a4YP4phqQ"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["titles_clean.columns"],"metadata":{"id":"L7Fqc_0rDv3X"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"code","source":["credits_clean.columns"],"metadata":{"id":"NlmtNoFHD4wE"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"1M8mcRywphqQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A horizontal bar chart is suitable because it makes it easy to compare the number of titles produced across different countries or regions. It also works well when there are many categories."],"metadata":{"id":"8agQvks0phqQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"tgIPom80phqQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["It will show which countries/regions contribute the highest number of Movies and TV Shows to the dataset. This can help identify the major content-producing markets and understand the geographical diversity of the content library."],"metadata":{"id":"Qp13pnNzphqQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 3. Will the gained insights help creating a positive business impact?\n","Are there any insights that lead to negative growth? Justify with specific reason."],"metadata":{"id":"JMzcOPDDphqR"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["Yes. The insight can support regional content planning, market analysis, and localization strategies. If some regions have very low content representation, that may indicate an opportunity to explore those markets further. However, low content representation does not automatically mean negative business growth, because the chart measures content count, not revenue, viewership, subscribers, or profitability."],"metadata":{"id":"R4Ka1PC2phqR"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart 11: Correlation Heatmap"],"metadata":{"id":"NC_X3p0fY2L0"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Correlation Heatmap visualization code\n","\n","# Select numerical columns\n","numeric_cols = [\n","    'release_year',\n","    'runtime',\n","    'seasons',\n","    'imdb_score',\n","    'imdb_votes',\n","    'tmdb_popularity',\n","    'tmdb_score'\n","]\n","\n","# Calculate correlation\n","corr = titles_clean[numeric_cols].corr()\n","\n","# Create heatmap\n","plt.figure(figsize=(10, 7))\n","\n","sns.heatmap(\n","    corr,\n","    annot=True,\n","    cmap='coolwarm',\n","    fmt='.2f'\n",")\n","\n","plt.title('Correlation Heatmap of Numerical Variables')\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"xyC9zolEZNRQ"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"UV0SzAkaZNRQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A correlation heatmap was chosen because it provides a clear way to compare the relationships between multiple numerical variables at the same time. The correlation values and colors make it easy to identify positive, negative, and weak relationships."],"metadata":{"id":"DVPuT8LYZNRQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"YPEH6qLeZNRQ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The strongest positive relationship is between IMDb score and TMDB score (0.58), indicating that titles rated higher on IMDb also tend to receive higher TMDB ratings. IMDb votes and TMDB popularity have a weak positive correlation (0.26), suggesting some relationship between audience voting activity and popularity. The strongest negative correlation is between release year and seasons (-0.41). Most other correlations are close to zero, indicating weak or no strong linear relationships between those variables."],"metadata":{"id":"bfSqtnDqZNRR"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### Chart - 12 - Pair Plot"],"metadata":{"id":"q29F0dvdveiT"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["# Pair Plot visualization code\n","\n","# Select important columns\n","pairplot_data = titles_clean[\n","    [\n","        'type',\n","        'imdb_score',\n","        'imdb_votes',\n","        'tmdb_popularity',\n","        'tmdb_score'\n","    ]\n","].dropna()\n","\n","# Create Pair Plot\n","sns.pairplot(\n","    data=pairplot_data,\n","    hue='type',\n","    diag_kind='hist'\n",")\n","\n","plt.suptitle(\n","    'Pair Plot of Content Performance Metrics',\n","    y=1.02\n",")\n","\n","plt.show()"],"metadata":{"id":"o58-TEIhveiU"},"execution_count":null,"outputs":[]},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 1. Why did you pick the specific chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"EXh0U9oCveiU"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["A pair plot was chosen because it allows us to analyze the relationships between multiple numerical variables simultaneously. It also helps compare Movies and TV Shows using different colors and shows the distribution of each variable along the diagonal."],"metadata":{"id":"eMmPjTByveiU"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["##### 2. What is/are the insight(s) found from the chart?"],"metadata":{"id":"22aHeOlLveiV"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["The pair plot shows several useful patterns:\n","\n","*   IMDb score and TMDB score show a noticeable positive relationship, supporting the correlation heatmap result that titles with higher IMDb ratings also tend to have higher TMDB ratings.\n","*   IMDb votes are highly skewed, with most titles receiving relatively fewer votes and a small number receiving very high vote counts.\n","*   TMDB popularity is also highly skewed, with a few titles having exceptionally high popularity compared with most titles.\n","*   Movies and TV Shows overlap considerably across the performance metrics, although TV Shows appear more concentrated toward higher rating ranges in some parts of the plot.\n","*   Overall, the plot suggests that ratings, popularity, and voting activity measure different aspects of content performance, and high popularity or a large number of votes does not necessarily guarantee a high rating."],"metadata":{"id":"uPQ8RGwHveiV"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["## **5. Solution to Business Objective**"],"metadata":{"id":"JcMwzZxoAimU"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["#### What do you suggest the client to achieve Business Objective ?\n","Explain Briefly."],"metadata":{"id":"8G2x9gOozGDZ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["*   Focus on Movies and TV Shows that have strong representation and audience relevance to maintain a balanced and attractive content library.\n","*   Invest more in popular and frequently occurring genres based on the genre analysis performed in the project.\n","*   Expand content in underrepresented regions and countries to improve Amazon Prime Video's global content presence.\n","*   Strengthen regional content by identifying countries that have potential for greater content acquisition and production.\n","*   Analyze content ratings to ensure that the platform provides suitable content for different audience segments.\n","*   Use release-year trends to understand changes in the content catalog and plan future content acquisition accordingly.\n","*   Identify gaps in the existing catalog by comparing genres, countries, ratings, and content types where content availability is relatively low.\n","*   Maintain a diverse content portfolio across different genres, regions, ratings, and content types instead of depending heavily on a limited number of categories.\n","\n","*   Leverage cast and director data from the credits dataset to identify frequently associated talent and support future content acquisition or production decisions.\n","\n","*   Use relationships between content attributes identified during the analysis to understand which characteristics commonly occur together and support better content planning.\n","\n","*   Regularly monitor the content catalog to identify changing trends and opportunities for adding relevant movies and TV shows.\n","\n","*   Create a data-driven content strategy using insights from genre, rating, country, release year, content type, cast, and director analysis.\n","\n","\n","*   Prioritize regional and genre expansion opportunities where the current catalog shows comparatively lower representation\n","\n","\n","*   Continuously evaluate the catalog using updated data so Amazon Prime Video can adapt its content strategy to changing viewer preferences.\n"],"metadata":{"id":"pASKb0qOza21"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["# **Conclusion**"],"metadata":{"id":"gCX9965dhzqZ"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["*   Movies are more prominent than TV Shows in the Amazon Prime Video content library.\n","\n","*   Content is concentrated in certain popular genres, indicating opportunities to strengthen both high-demand and underrepresented genres.\n","\n","*   The catalog shows strong regional variation, with some countries contributing significantly more content than others.\n","\n","*   Content availability has changed over the years, highlighting the expansion and evolution of the Prime Video catalog.\n","\n","*   Ratings and content characteristics vary across titles, showing that Amazon Prime Video serves different audience segments.\n","\n","*   Genre, rating, country, and content-type relationships provide useful insights for improving content acquisition and production decisions.\n","\n","*   The credits analysis highlights recurring actors and directors, which can support future talent and content strategy decisions.\n","\n","*   Overall, the analysis can help Amazon Prime Video identify content gaps, regional opportunities, and genre trends to build a more diverse and data-driven content library."],"metadata":{"id":"Fjb1IsQkh3yE"}},{"cell_type":"markdown","source":["### ***Hurrah! You have successfully completed your EDA Capstone Project !!!***"],"metadata":{"id":"gIfDvo9L0UH2"}},{"cell_type":"code","source":["titles_clean.to_csv(\"amazon_prime_titles_clean.csv\", index=False)\n","credits_clean.to_csv(\"amazon_prime_credits_cle